WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.284
Hello, and welcome to week two: exchange and subtract.

2
00:00:05.284 --> 00:00:09.870
By the end, you will be able to subtract in columns when you need to exchange.

3
00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:12.095
Let's start.

4
00:00:13.245 --> 00:00:16.322
We are taking eighteen away from fifty-three.

5
00:00:16.322 --> 00:00:17.877
Start with the ones.

6
00:00:17.877 --> 00:00:22.324
There are three ones, and we need to take away eight ones.

7
00:00:22.324 --> 00:00:25.363
There are not enough ones.

8
00:00:27.263 --> 00:00:33.892
There are not enough ones to take away eight ones, so I exchange one ten for ten ones.

9
00:00:33.892 --> 00:00:37.259
Now there are four tens and thirteen ones.

10
00:00:37.259 --> 00:00:39.705
It is still fifty-three.

11
00:00:41.605 --> 00:00:45.216
Take away eight ones, then one ten.

12
00:00:45.216 --> 00:00:47.038
Write the answer.

13
00:00:47.038 --> 00:00:50.732
Pause the video and have a go.

14
00:00:59.382 --> 00:01:02.679
Thirteen ones take away eight ones is five ones.

15
00:01:02.679 --> 00:01:06.360
Four tens take away one ten is three tens.

16
00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:10.338
Fifty-three take away eighteen is thirty-five.

17
00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:14.641
The same idea, one place up:

18
00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:19.448
three hundred and twenty-five subtract one hundred and seventy-two.

19
00:01:19.448 --> 00:01:21.224
The ones are fine.

20
00:01:21.224 --> 00:01:24.080
Exchange one hundred for ten tens.

21
00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:27.681
Pause the video and have a go.

22
00:01:36.331 --> 00:01:40.035
Ones: five take away two is three.

23
00:01:40.035 --> 00:01:44.284
Tens: there are not enough tens to take away seven tens,

24
00:01:44.284 --> 00:01:47.175
so I exchange one hundred for ten tens.

25
00:01:47.175 --> 00:01:51.540
Twelve tens take away seven tens is five tens.

26
00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:54.640
Two hundreds take away one hundred is one hundred.

27
00:01:54.640 --> 00:02:02.194
Three hundred and twenty-five take away one hundred and seventy-two is one hundred and fifty-three.

28
00:02:04.094 --> 00:02:06.416
Here is a worked example.

29
00:02:06.416 --> 00:02:12.635
Calculate three hundred and eighty-one subtract one hundred and forty-seven.

30
00:02:13.885 --> 00:02:20.805
Ones: there are not enough ones to take away seven ones, so I exchange one ten for ten ones.

31
00:02:20.805 --> 00:02:23.556
Eleven subtract seven equals four.

32
00:02:23.556 --> 00:02:27.689
Tens: seven subtract four equals three.

33
00:02:27.689 --> 00:02:32.228
Hundreds: three subtract one equals two.

34
00:02:32.228 --> 00:02:40.054
Three hundred and eighty-one subtract one hundred and forty-seven equals two hundred and thirty-four.

35
00:02:40.054 --> 00:02:42.457
Pause the video.

36
00:02:42.457 --> 00:02:45.815
Try the next one in your booklet.

37
00:02:55.115 --> 00:02:56.973
Now let's try a question together.

38
00:02:56.973 --> 00:03:01.884
Calculate three hundred and eighteen subtract one hundred and sixty-three.

39
00:03:01.884 --> 00:03:04.892
Pause the video and have a go.

40
00:03:13.542 --> 00:03:16.712
Ones: eight subtract three equals five.

41
00:03:16.712 --> 00:03:20.543
Tens: there are not enough tens to take away six tens,

42
00:03:20.543 --> 00:03:23.561
so I exchange one hundred for ten tens.

43
00:03:23.561 --> 00:03:26.394
Eleven subtract six equals five.

44
00:03:26.394 --> 00:03:31.120
Hundreds: two subtract one equals one.

45
00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:37.644
Three hundred and eighteen subtract one hundred and sixty-three equals one hundred and fifty-five.

46
00:03:37.644 --> 00:03:40.195
Well done if you got it.

47
00:03:42.095 --> 00:03:44.069
Now try it in your booklet.

48
00:03:44.069 --> 00:03:46.472
Remember: start with the ones.

49
00:03:46.472 --> 00:03:48.585
If the top digit is too small,

50
00:03:48.585 --> 00:03:54.750
exchange one ten for ten ones (or one hundred for ten tens), then take away.

51
00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:56.302
Good luck.
